I think a lot of companies are seeing  the importance and the value of Hosting  Retreats now especially after two years  of covid where there is a growing sense  of isolation  [Music]  my name is Sean Hoff I'm the managing  partner of moniker a lot of companies  that either gave up their office during  covid and moved to a fully remote model  or a hybrid model have reached out to us  and asked we could help them plan their  first Retreat you see their names on  slack or they pop up in your email all  the time but being able to put that face  to the name and allowing you to actually  develop that relationship we've just  anecdotally seen people write in after  on the post-trip surveys talking about  how reinvigorated and re-energized they  feel after the retreat having been able  to kind of reconnect with their  colleagues the tools and our ability to  work remotely has made it possible to  build what we've built but the human  connection piece of it is vital to what  we do and the Retreats just amplify that  a million fold every time we do them for  us these Retreats have become probably  our number one retention tool because  people grow closer together they  understand each other more they end up  working better together because of it  and the excitement level goes through  the roof and it has this halo effect  that lasts for the rest of the year if  we do them right my advice is is they're  done right and you go in with the right  attitude and you actually really care  about them the return is absolutely  no-brainer  [Music]  somebody will find us either through a  referral and get connected to us  directly or they just find us on the  internet and we'll have a conversation  talking a little bit about what it is  that they're looking to do whether it be  a short celebration type Retreat or if  it's going to be like a few days abroad  where there's a mix of work and some fun  from there we would put together a  proposal sharing three to five  destinations talking 