 optional activity where the group can  get together and actually just you know  have some fun together we work together  on the theme we'll lean into that and  then create games and contests and other  events along the way to tie into that  and really make it feel like a cohesive  over-the-top experience biggest thing is  to deliver Happiness joy and emotion so  no matter what the activity it is it can  be a simple wine tasting it can be a  cooking class or maybe a sort of game  with the cars like we did with Sean  [Music]  there's this company Plex that we've  worked with for many years one of my  favorite activities that we planned we  took them to Tuscany back in 2016. they  were looking for for something to get  people out exploring the region we  staged essentially The Italian Job a  bank heist so we told the group to come  meet us in the parking lot and sure  enough their version of like the special  police comes tearing down the driveway  Sirens blazing and he pulls through a  stop in front of them and he gets out  and everybody's looking at each other  having no idea what's going on and he  basically starts to explain that there's  been a robbery in the nearby town of  Monte San Savino and their police force  is small and they heard that this group  was in town and hopefully they could  help enlist them to solve this crime  they drive Monte San Savino and we had  an actor with his wrists bound and tape  over his mouth sitting in front of this  Bank these attendees walk up they take  the tape off and he says yes yes I was  just robbed there were three people who  just left this bank and as they were  leaving this piece of paper dropped out  of their back pocket and it just kind of  evolved into this really fun circuit  with a whole bunch of diversions and  side quests was just an awesome way to  explore the destination that we were in  but at the same time bring the team  together  foreign  [Music]  ly think that the industry around  Retreats and off sites i